---
import WysBuyerFrame from '../../../../components/WysBuyerFrame.astro';
import {WYS_BUYER_ROOT, AFF, UPDATES} from '../../../../data/wys-buyer.js';
import {Image} from 'astro:assets';
import roundupExample from '../../../../lifestyle/wys-example-roundup-gamer.jpg';
---
<WysBuyerFrame title="Start Here" current="start">
 <header class="wb2-hero">
  <div class="wys-wrap">
   <p class="wb2-kicker">You're in · Start here</p>
   <h1>The While-You-Sleep Storefront™</h1>
   <p>Set it up once. Every night after that it plans the looks, sources them on Amazon, makes the photos, writes the posts and schedules everything. You sleep.</p>
  </div>
 </header>

 <section class="wb2-sec" id="new-approved" style="padding-bottom:0">
  <div class="wys-wrap">
   <div class="wb2-note" style="border-style:solid;border-width:2px;padding:20px 22px">
    <p class="wb2-kicker" style="margin:0 0 6px">New · 23 October 2026</p>
    <h2 style="margin:0 0 8px">Not an Amazon Influencer yet? Start here</h2>
    <p style="margin:0 0 14px">The new Get Approved page takes you from no Amazon account to your own storefront: Associate vs Influencer, onsite vs offsite, what to fix before you apply, how to apply, and what to set up the day you're approved. Only have Associates? Your system already runs while you wait.</p>
    <a class="wb2-btn" href={WYS_BUYER_ROOT + '/get-approved'}>Get approved <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
   </div>
  </div>
 </section>

 <section class="wb2-sec" id="new-roundup" style="padding-bottom:0">
  <div class="wys-wrap">
   <div class="wb2-note" style="border-style:solid;border-width:2px;padding:20px 22px;display:flex;gap:20px;align-items:flex-start;flex-wrap:wrap">
    <div style="flex:1 1 280px;min-width:0">
     <p class="wb2-kicker" style="margin:0 0 6px">New · 23 October 2026</p>
     <h2 style="margin:0 0 8px">Two new pins for every look: the Roundup and the Found It</h2>
     <p style="margin:0 0 10px">Every piece of the look together in one styled scene, with a three-line headline across the top, like the "You'll Love This Year" roundup pins all over Pinterest. Plus the Found It: the look's most interesting piece on its own in a real, lived-in photo, with handwritten "I found this on Amazon" words over it. Both link straight to the look's Idea List. Pick which ones you want: Set It Up now asks which pins to make for every look. Already set up? It takes two minutes:</p>
     <ol style="margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:22px">
      <li>Open Set It Up. If you set up on this computer, your answers are still filled in.</li>
      <li>Under Pinterest, tick the pins you want for every look.</li>
      <li>Copy your new nightly run and tell Claude: "Replace my While-You-Sleep nightly run task's prompt with this."</li>
     </ol>
     <a class="wb2-btn" href={WYS_BUYER_ROOT + '/set-it-up'}>Get my new nightly run <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
    <Image src={roundupExample} alt="Example Roundup pin: a pink gamer girl desk under the headline Pink Gamer Girl, Desk Setup, Cute Enough to Stream" widths={[240, 480]} sizes="220px" style="width:220px;height:auto;border-radius:12px;flex:none"/>
   </div>
  </div>
 </section>

 <section class="wb2-sec" id="new-characters" style="padding-bottom:0">
  <div class="wys-wrap">
   <div class="wb2-note" style="border-style:solid;border-width:2px;padding:20px 22px">
    <p class="wb2-kicker" style="margin:0 0 6px">New · 19 October 2026</p>
    <h2 style="margin:0 0 8px">Add your favorite licensed characters</h2>
    <p style="margin:0 0 10px">Your storefront can now use licensed characters: Hello Kitty, Kuromi, My Melody, Barbie, Stitch, Snoopy and more. If it's sold on Amazon, it's allowed, and it shows up in your photos exactly like the listing. Already set up? It takes about two minutes:</p>
    <ol style="margin:0 0 12px;padding-left:22px">
     <li>Open Set It Up. If you set up on this computer, your answers are still filled in.</li>
     <li>Under Categories, tick "Licensed characters and fandom favorites". Then tick your favorites under "Your favorite licensed characters".</li>
     <li>Copy your new nightly run and tell Claude: "Replace my While-You-Sleep nightly run task's prompt with this."</li>
    </ol>
    <p style="margin:0 0 14px">Don't want characters? Skip this. Nothing changes until you tick them.</p>
    <a class="wb2-btn" href={WYS_BUYER_ROOT + '/set-it-up'}>Add my characters <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
   </div>
  </div>
 </section>

 <section class="wb2-sec">
  <div class="wys-wrap">
   <h2>What it makes every night</h2>
   <p>This is my own storefront's nightly output on the default settings. You can run one look a night instead to halve the credits.</p>
   <div class="wb2-night">
    <div><strong>2</strong><span>complete looks, sourced and listed</span></div>
    <div><strong>6</strong><span>Pinterest pins, scheduled</span></div>
    <div><strong>2</strong><span>blog posts on your site</span></div>
    <div><strong>2</strong><span>Instagram carousels</span></div>
   </div>
  </div>
 </section>

 <section class="wb2-sec" style="background:#fff">
  <div class="wys-wrap">
   <h2>Three steps, then hands off</h2>
   <div class="wb2-grid">
    <div class="wb2-card"><span class="wb2-n">1</span><h3>Answer the questions</h3><p>On the Set It Up page. Quick Start is about 15 minutes. Making it fully yours is about an hour. Your answers build your own setup and nightly prompts, ready to copy.</p></div>
    <div class="wb2-card"><span class="wb2-n">2</span><h3>Paste one prompt</h3><p>Paste your setup prompt into a new Claude chat. It checks every connection, then makes your first look with you watching so you can correct it.</p></div>
    <div class="wb2-card"><span class="wb2-n">3</span><h3>It turns itself on</h3><p>When you say it's right, it creates the nightly scheduled task. From then on it runs at the time you picked, every night.</p></div>
   </div>
   <p class="wb2-note"><b>My advice:</b> keep approvals on for your first few days. Every pin and carousel waits in Metricool for your OK. Turn approvals off once you trust it.</p>
   <p style="margin-top:18px"><a class="wb2-btn" href={WYS_BUYER_ROOT + '/set-it-up'}>Go to Set It Up <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
  </div>
 </section>

 <section class="wb2-sec">
  <div class="wys-wrap">
   <h2>What you need</h2>
   <p>Get these ready before you paste anything. Prices are each company's own and can change, so check them on their sites.</p>
   <div class="wb2-grid">
    <div class="wb2-card must"><span class="wb2-tag">Runs it</span><h3>Claude</h3><p>A paid Claude plan with scheduled tasks, and the Claude desktop app on your computer. The nightly run happens on your computer, so it stays on and the app stays open overnight.</p></div>
    <div class="wb2-card must"><span class="wb2-tag">Shops it</span><h3>Amazon</h3><p>Amazon Influencer (your storefront and Idea Lists) or Amazon Associates. Sign in to Amazon once in the browser inside the Claude desktop app and stay signed in. Not approved yet? <a href={WYS_BUYER_ROOT + '/get-approved'}>Get Approved</a> walks you through it.</p></div>
    <div class="wb2-card must"><span class="wb2-tag">Schedules it</span><h3>Metricool</h3><p>For loading and scheduling your pins and posts automatically. The free plan is fine to start; you’ll want to upgrade once you scale up. Connect your Pinterest business account (and Instagram, if you want carousels), then add the Metricool connector in Claude.</p></div>
    <div class="wb2-card must"><span class="wb2-tag">Makes the photos</span><h3>Higgsfield</h3><p>A Higgsfield plan with credits, and the Higgsfield connector in Claude. Each look uses about 3 credits on the default models. <a href={AFF.higgsfield} target="_blank" rel="sponsored noopener">Get Higgsfield here</a> (my affiliate link).</p></div>
    <div class="wb2-card must"><span class="wb2-tag">Remembers it</span><h3>Google Drive</h3><p>Free. Add the Google Drive connector in Claude. Your log lives here, so it never repeats a look and always remembers your corrections.</p></div>
    <div class="wb2-card"><span class="wb2-tag">Optional</span><h3>Your own site</h3><p>For blog posts. Any website works if you paste the posts in yourself. For automatic posts it needs to live on GitHub, plus the GitHub connector in Claude. No site yet? <a href={AFF.weekendEcosystem}>The Weekend Ecosystem™</a> builds one.</p></div>
   </div>
  </div>
 </section>

 <section class="wb2-sec" style="background:#fff">
  <div class="wys-wrap">
   <h2>Every option is yours</h2>
   <p>The main path is fully automatic. Every one of these is a switch on the Set It Up page, and you can mix and match.</p>
   <div class="wb2-grid">
    <div class="wb2-card"><h3>Approvals</h3><p>On: every pin and carousel waits in Metricool for your OK. Off: fully automatic.</p></div>
    <div class="wb2-card"><h3>One look a night</h3><p>Half the credits and half the Claude usage. Half the pins, half the photos.</p></div>
    <div class="wb2-card"><h3>No face</h3><p>No persona? Lifestyle photos show hands and the products in use.</p></div>
    <div class="wb2-card"><h3>Any step by hand</h3><p>Pick the products yourself, make the photos on the Higgsfield website, schedule pins in Pinterest, post the carousels or paste the blog posts yourself. It writes everything you need into your log.</p></div>
    <div class="wb2-card"><h3>Instagram on or off</h3><p>One carousel per look at the time you pick, in the photo order you pick.</p></div>
    <div class="wb2-card"><h3>Credit limit</h3><p>Set a monthly cap. When it's reached, it stops making photos and tells you. It never switches models behind your back.</p></div>
   </div>
  </div>
 </section>

 <section class="wb2-sec">
  <div class="wys-wrap">
   <h2>What's new</h2>
   <p>This site gets updated as things change, and new affiliate platforms are on the way. Check back here.</p>
   <ul class="wb2-updates">{UPDATES.map((u) => <li><b>{u.date}</b>{u.text}</li>)}</ul>
  </div>
 </section>
</WysBuyerFrame>
